  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 130 PM CDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nA broad mid level trough across the western gulf combined with a \nstalled frontal boundary along the TX coast will continue to bring \nscattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms to the Middle Texas \nCoastal Waters through mid week. However, rain chances will diminish \nacross S TX tonight through Monday as the stalled front drifts \nfarther out into the gulf and a mid level ridge nudges across S TX. \nQuiet weather is in store for Monday through Wednesday, then Rain \nchances return later in the week as a mid level low approaches S TX \nand pushes the ridge southward.\n\nMinor coastal flooding is expected during times of high tide through \nTuesday, possibly into Wednesday. This is due to a moderate to \nstrong northeast flow across the northwest gulf waters. High tides \nwill vary from overnight into morning at Baffin Bay and in the \nmorning to afternoon at Port Oconnor, thus tidal overflow may be \nsomewhat continuous over the next couple of days.",
